From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Recognize riscv on desktop Linux

kCpuArchitecture is a telemetry string, and the ladder that sets it ends in
#error, so an architecture it does not name cannot build at all. Same shape as
the arm patch before it.

__riscv_xlen separates the two: the toolchain defines __riscv for both.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
---
--- a/app/src/app_common.cc
+++ b/app/src/app_common.cc
@@ -159,6 +159,10 @@
 const char* kCpuArchitecture = "arm64";
 #elif __arm__
 const char* kCpuArchitecture = "arm";
+#elif defined(__riscv) && __riscv_xlen == 64
+const char* kCpuArchitecture = "riscv64";
+#elif defined(__riscv) && __riscv_xlen == 32
+const char* kCpuArchitecture = "riscv32";
 #else
 #error Unknown Linux architecture.
 #endif  // Architecture
